module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatRelations
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.Free
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.Submodule
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Flat.EquationalCriterion
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The equational criterion for flatness: a flat sheaf of modules satisfies it

Let `(C, O)` be a ringed site and let `F` be a sheaf of `O`-modules. Stacks 08FC characterises
flatness of `F` by a local factorisation property of the relations among its sections; part (2)
of the source is the case of a single relation and part (3) the case of a finite matrix of
relations. Their equivalence is
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatRelations`
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.hasLocalSingleRelationFactorizations_iff_finite`).

This file proves the implication (1) `⟹` (2) of the source,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.hasLocalSingleRelationFactorizations_of_isFlat_freeUniverse`: a flat sheaf
of modules satisfies the single-relation criterion, for a structure sheaf whose sections lie in a
universe independent of the universes of the site. The converse is not proved here. Three things
are needed and all are supplied here.

* The **universal relation presheaf** for relations of a given length `n`. Stacks works with the
  sheaf of ideals `I ⊆ O_U` generated by `a₁, …, a_n` on the localised site `C/U`. Localisation
  is avoided here, and so is any reference to `U`: the relation is recorded *universally*, as the
  subpresheaf `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tupleSubmodule` of the free presheaf of `O`-modules on the
  presheaf `Stacks.SheafOfModules.coeffTuples` of `n`-tuples of sections, generated over each
  object `X` by the sections `bᵢ • e_b` for every tuple `b` of sections over `X`. The relation at
  hand is the component indexed by the tuple `a` itself. The point of passing to a free presheaf
  rather than staying inside `O` is that the component indexed by a fixed tuple is then a *direct
  summand* (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.tupleProj`), whereas inside `O` the spans attached to
  different tuples overlap and the relation one reads off would involve all of them at once.

* The **local algebraic step** `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_relFactorization`: once the
  relation element is known to vanish in `relSubmodule a ⊗ F` over `V`, the sections `s` factor
  through a finite free module by a matrix annihilating the restricted relation. This is where
  Mathlib's equational criterion for the vanishing of a tensor
  (`TensorProduct.vanishesTrivially_of_sum_tmul_eq_zero_of_rTensor_injective`, Stacks 04VX)
  is applied, with the required injectivity coming from the splitting just described.

* A **bridge from monomorphisms to local injectivity**
  (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_of_mono_shf_map`): a morphism of presheaves of
  modules whose sheafification is a monomorphism is locally injective. This is the form in
  which the flatness hypothesis of part (1) is consumed.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.coeffTuples`: the presheaf of `n`-tuples of sections of the structure
  sheaf.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeTuples`: the free presheaf of `O`-modules on `coeffTuples O n`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tupleGen`: the section of `freeTuples O n` over `X` supported in the
  component indexed by a tuple `b`, with coefficient the `i`-th entry of `b`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tupleSubmodule`: the subpresheaf of `freeTuples O n` generated by the
  `tupleGen`; this is the universal form of the extension by zero of the ideal sheaf of the
  source.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tupleCoeff` and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tupleProj`: the coefficient of,
  and the projection onto, the component indexed by a fixed tuple.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.uliftYoneda`: `Hom(-, U)`, with its values lifted into the universe of
  the sections of the structure sheaf.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeOn`: the free presheaf of `O`-modules on `Hom(-, U)`, i.e. the
  extension by zero of the structure sheaf of the localised site `C/U`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.relGen`: the section of `freeOn O U` over `V` supported in the
  component indexed by `g : V ⟶ U`, with coefficient the restriction of `a i` along `g`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.relSubmodule`: the subpresheaf of `freeOn O U` generated by the
  `relGen`; this is the extension by zero of the ideal sheaf of the source.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.relCoeff` and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.relProj`: the coefficient of, and
  the projection onto, the component indexed by a fixed arrow.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shf`, `shfRight`, `shfAdj`: sheafification of presheaves of
  `O`-modules, its right adjoint and the adjunction.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shfUnit`: the unit of that adjunction, with its target spelled as the
  underlying presheaf of modules of the sheafification.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorRightOf`: tensoring presheaves of `O`-modules on the right by
  the underlying presheaf of a sheaf of `O`-modules.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.hasLocalSingleRelationFactorizations_of_isFlat_freeUniverse`:
  a flat sheaf of modules satisfies the single-relation criterion, at a section universe
  independent of the universes of the site.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_tupleFactorization`: the local algebraic step described above.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_covering_tupleFactorization`: that step spread over a covering,
  the covering being the equalizer sieve of the relation element.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tupleProj_mem_span`: the projection onto the component of a fixed tuple
  maps the relation subpresheaf into the submodule generated by that component's generators.
  This is the splitting which makes the local algebraic step applicable.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.span_tupleGen_mk_eq_top`: over each object the relation subpresheaf is
  spanned by the `tupleGen`, which is what lets the splitting be checked on generators.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_relFactorization`,
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_covering_relFactorization`,
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.relProj_mem_span` and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.span_relGen_mk_eq_top`: the
  same four statements for the earlier `Hom(-, U)`-indexed construction; see the implementation
  notes.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_of_mono_shf_map`: the monomorphism-to-local
  injectivity bridge.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map`: flatness of `F` turns a monomorphism of
  *presheaves* of modules into one whose sheafification stays a monomorphism after tensoring with
  `F`. Together with the bridge above this is where the hypothesis of part (1) is used.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map_val`: the sheaf-level tensor functor
  `(Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor O).flip.obj F`, whose exactness *is* flatness,
  preserves monomorphisms; its action on a morphism `v` is `shf ∘ tensorRightOf` applied to
  `v.val` by definition.

## Implementation notes

The hypotheses are exactly those under which `Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsFlat` is stated, namely
`HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat` and `J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat`; no left
exactness of sheafification is assumed. The step which looks as though it needed it — turning the
monomorphism `relSubmodule a ↪ freeOn O U` of presheaves of modules into a monomorphism of
sheaves of modules — is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_shf_map`, and it goes through local
injectivity and `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.mono_of_isLocallyInjective` instead of through
`PreservesFiniteLimits (PresheafOfModules.sheafification α)`, which would have forced the
stronger `HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat`.

The universe of the sections of the structure sheaf is an independent `w`, unrelated to the
morphism universe `v` of the site. That is what lets the two halves of Stacks 08FC be paired in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatEquivalenceIff`, the converse half already
being stated at an independent `w`.

Indexing the relation presheaf by *tuples of sections* rather than by *arrows into `U`* is what
buys that. The earlier construction in this file — `Stacks.SheafOfModules.uliftYoneda`, `freeOn`,
`relGen`, `relSubmodule`, `relCoeff`, `relProj` and the factorisation lemmas over them —
realises the extension by zero `j_! I` as a subpresheaf of the free presheaf on `Hom(-, U)`,
whose index type lives in the morphism universe `v`. Since `PresheafOfModules.freeObj` sends a
`Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type t` to a `PresheafOfModules.{t}` over a `Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{t}`, that pins the sections of
`O` to `max v w`; and the flatness hypothesis, being exactness of the tensor endofunctor of
sheaves of modules at the section universe, is then not available at the universe the free
presheaf lives in. Those declarations are kept, at `max v w`, but they are no longer on the path
to the main theorem: `coeffTuples O n` carries the same splitting argument with an index type in
`Type w`, because `Fin n → O(X)` is as small as `O(X)`.

Everything in the final section — sheafification of presheaves of modules, its unit, the
monomorphism bridge and the consumption of flatness — merely *carries* the section universe, and
is stated at the independent one with no change to any proof.

The ring presheaf is spelled `Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj` in the construction and the algebraic
step, and `(Stacks.commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj` in the sheafification material. The two are
equal by `rfl`, but only the first lets typeclass search find the `CommRing` instance on the
sections, and that instance is what the tensor product of modules and Mathlib's
`TensorProduct.VanishesTrivially` require; the second is the spelling under which
`SheafOfModules` and the sheaf-level tensor functor of flatness are stated.

Crossing between the two spellings is affordable during *elaboration*, where `isDefEq` may
unfold `CategoryTheory.sheafCompose`, but it is impossible during *typeclass search*, which runs
at `instances` transparency and cannot unfold a plain definition. That is why the crossing is
confined to a handful of declarations which name the offending instances outright
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_id_commRingSheafToRingSheaf`,
`isLocallyInjective_shfUnit` and their companions) or take them as explicit arguments
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_of_square`, `mono_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map`). Spelling
`commRingSheafToRingSheaf O` as an explicit pair `⟨ringPresheaf O.obj, _⟩` would make typeclass
search succeed at both spellings, but making `(…).obj` reduce changes the discrimination-tree
key of every goal mentioning it, and
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ModuleStalkFunctor` then loses the instance
`Stacks.instPreservesFiniteLimitsSheafModuleFiber`, which is keyed on `R.obj` for a variable `R`.

Several proofs are written as explicit `Eq.trans` chains rather than with `rw`. The reason is the
same crossing: `rw` has to check that its motive is type-correct at `implicit` transparency, and
a term mixing the two spellings — or mixing `(relSubmodule a).obj X` with
`(relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules.obj X` — is not. Each step is also kept in its own
declaration rather than as a `have`, because `maxHeartbeats` is a per-declaration budget and the
crossings are individually affordable but not collectively.

`tupleCoeff`, `tupleProj` and their `relCoeff`, `relProj` counterparts are defined by
`show ... from` on `Finsupp.lapply` and `Finsupp.lsingle` rather than by `LinearMap.mk`, because
the module structure that `ModuleCat.of` carries on `ι →₀ R` and the one `Finsupp` carries are
definitionally equal but not syntactically so; going through `show` fixes a single spelling for
the rest of the file.

`Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeTuples_map_tupleGen` is a term-mode `Eq.trans` rather than a `rw`, for
the same reason the file's other chains are: the two spellings `Fin n → O(X)` and
`(coeffTuples O n).obj X` of the index type are definitionally but not syntactically equal, so
`rw` rejects its own motive as ill-typed at `implicit` transparency, while `congrArg` and `exact`
tolerate the crossing.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08FC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08FC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04VX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04VX)

Tags covered: 08FC (part (1) implies part (2)).
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe w v u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

section TensorAlgebra

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {M N P : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
  [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] [AddCommGroup P] [Module R P]

/-- Tensoring a split injection with a fixed module gives an injection. -/
lemma injective_rTensor_of_retraction (f : M →ₗ[R] N) (r : N →ₗ[R] M)
    (hr : ∀ x, r (f x) = x) :
    Function.Injective (LinearMap.rTensor P f) := by
  intro x y hxy
  have h := congrArg (LinearMap.rTensor P r) hxy
  rw [← LinearMap.comp_apply, ← LinearMap.comp_apply, ← LinearMap.rTensor_comp] at h
  rw [show r ∘ₗ f = LinearMap.id from LinearMap.ext hr, LinearMap.rTensor_id] at h
  simpa using h

/-- A family of elements of a module, viewed inside the submodule it spans, spans it. -/
lemma span_range_mk_eq_top {ι : Type*} (m : ι → M) :
    Submodule.span R (Set.range fun i : ι ↦
        (⟨m i, Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩⟩ : Submodule.span R (Set.range m))) = ⊤ := by
  rw [eq_top_iff]
  rintro ⟨x, hx⟩ -
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x h =>
    obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := h
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩
  | zero => exact zero_mem _
  | add x y hx hy ihx ihy => exact add_mem ihx ihy
  | smul r x hx ih => exact Submodule.smul_mem _ r ih

/-- If a combination `∑ᵢ rᵢ • nᵢ` vanishes, then so does `∑ᵢ (rᵢ • m) ⊗ nᵢ` for every `m`: the
scalars can be moved across the tensor sign and collected. -/
lemma sum_smul_tmul_eq_zero {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (r : ι → R) (m : M) (n : ι → N)
    (h : ∑ i, r i • n i = 0) :
    ∑ i, (r i • m) ⊗ₜ[R] n i = 0 := by
  have e : ∑ i, (r i • m) ⊗ₜ[R] n i = m ⊗ₜ[R] ∑ i, r i • n i := by
    rw [TensorProduct.tmul_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
    rw [← TensorProduct.smul_tmul', TensorProduct.tmul_smul]
  rw [e, h, TensorProduct.tmul_zero]

/-- Equational criterion for a submodule `S` generated by `m` over a retraction `ψ`: if `ψ` maps
`S` into the span of `m` and fixes `m`, and `∑ᵢ mᵢ ⊗ sᵢ` vanishes in `S ⊗ F`, then `s` factors
through a finite free module by a matrix annihilating `(c (mᵢ))ᵢ`, for any functional `c`. -/
private theorem exists_factorization_of_retraction {A F : Type*} [AddCommGroup A] [Module R A]
    [AddCommGroup F] [Module R F] {n : ℕ} (S : Submodule R A) (m : Fin n → A)
    (hm : ∀ i, m i ∈ S) (ψ : A →ₗ[R] A) (c : A →ₗ[R] R) (d : Fin n → R)
    (hfix : ∀ i, ψ (m i) = m i) (hψ : ∀ y ∈ S, ψ y ∈ Submodule.span R (Set.range m))
    (hc : ∀ i, c (m i) = d i) (s : Fin n → F)
    (h : ∑ i, (⟨m i, hm i⟩ : S) ⊗ₜ[R] s i = 0) :
    ∃ (l : ℕ) (t : Fin l → F) (B : Fin l → Fin n → R),
      (∀ i, s i = ∑ k, B k i • t k) ∧ (∀ k, ∑ i, B k i * d i = 0) := by
  set Qv := Submodule.span R (Set.range fun i ↦ (⟨m i, hm i⟩ : S)) with hQv
  have hψ₀ : ∀ y : S, ψ y ∈ S := fun y ↦
    Submodule.span_le.mpr (by rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩; exact hm i) (hψ y y.2)
  set ψ' : S →ₗ[R] S := LinearMap.codRestrict S (ψ ∘ₗ S.subtype) hψ₀ with hψ'
  have hψQ : ∀ y : S, ψ' y ∈ Qv := fun y ↦ by
    obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := (Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun R).1 (hψ y y.2)
    have : ψ' y = ∑ i, e i • (⟨m i, hm i⟩ : S) := Subtype.ext <| by
      simp only [Submodule.coe_sum, Submodule.coe_smul]; exact he.symm
    exact this ▸ sum_mem fun i _ ↦ Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)
  have hρ : ∀ q : Qv, (LinearMap.codRestrict Qv ψ' hψQ) (Qv.subtype q) = q := fun q ↦ by
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    have : ∀ y ∈ Qv, ψ' y = y := fun y hy ↦ by
      induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
      | mem z hz => obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hz; exact Subtype.ext (hfix i)
      | zero => exact map_zero _
      | add z z' hz hz' ihz ihz' => rw [map_add, ihz, ihz']
      | smul r z hz ih => rw [map_smul, ih]
    exact this q.1 q.2
  obtain ⟨l, B, t, h1, h2⟩ :=
    TensorProduct.vanishesTrivially_of_sum_tmul_eq_zero_of_rTensor_injective R
      (injective_rTensor_of_retraction Qv.subtype (LinearMap.codRestrict Qv ψ' hψQ) hρ) h
  refine ⟨l, t, fun k i ↦ B i k, h1, fun k ↦ ?_⟩
  have h3 := congrArg (c ∘ₗ S.subtype) (h2 k)
  simpa [hc] using h3

end TensorAlgebra

section CommSq

/-- The image of a commuting square under two successive functors is a commuting square. Stated
for a composite of two functors, rather than for their composition, so that it applies to a goal
in which the two functors appear separately. -/
lemma functor_map_square {D E K : Type*} [Category D] [Category E] [Category K]
    (T : D ⥤ E) (S : E ⥤ K) {P Q P' Q' : D} {u : P ⟶ Q} {ηP : P ⟶ P'} {ηQ : Q ⟶ Q'}
    {w : P' ⟶ Q'} (sq : u ≫ ηQ = ηP ≫ w) :
    S.map (T.map u) ≫ S.map (T.map ηQ) = S.map (T.map ηP) ≫ S.map (T.map w) := by
  rw [← S.map_comp, ← T.map_comp, sq, T.map_comp, S.map_comp]

/-- In a commuting square whose left and bottom edges are monomorphisms, the top edge is a
monomorphism. The two monomorphism assumptions are explicit arguments rather than instances
because at the point of use they have to be supplied by hand. -/
lemma mono_of_square {K : Type*} [Category K] {A B A' B' : K} {f : A ⟶ B} {g : A ⟶ A'}
    {h : B ⟶ B'} {k : A' ⟶ B'} (sq : f ≫ h = g ≫ k) (hg : Mono g) (hk : Mono k) : Mono f := by
  have := hg
  have := hk
  exact mono_of_mono_fac sq

end CommSq

section Construction

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- `Hom(-, U)`, with its values lifted into the universe of the sections of the
structure sheaf. -/
@[simps]
def uliftYoneda (U : C) : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (max v w) where
  obj X := ULift.{w} (X.unop ⟶ U)
  map {X Y} h := ↾fun (x : ULift.{w} (X.unop ⟶ U)) ↦ (ULift.up (h.unop ≫ x.down) :
    ULift.{w} (Y.unop ⟶ U))

variable (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{max v w})

/-- The free presheaf of `O`-modules on `Hom(-, U)`. -/
noncomputable abbrev freeOn (U : C) :
    PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj) :=
  PresheafOfModules.freeObj (R := ringPresheaf O.obj) (uliftYoneda.{w} U)

variable {O}

/-- The section of `freeOn O U` over `X` supported in the component indexed by `g : X ⟶ U`,
with coefficient the restriction of `a i` along `g`. -/
noncomputable def relGen {U : C} {n : ℕ}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) (g : X.unop ⟶ U) (i : Fin n) : (freeOn O U).obj X :=
  ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map g.op).hom (a i) •
    (ModuleCat.freeMk (ULift.up g : (uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj X) : (freeOn O U).obj X)

/-- `relGen a X g i` is the finitely supported function at `g` with value the restriction of
`a i` along `g`. -/
lemma relGen_eq_single {U : C} {n : ℕ} (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) (g : X.unop ⟶ U) (i : Fin n) :
    relGen a X g i = Finsupp.single (ULift.up g : (uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj X)
      (((ringPresheaf O.obj).map g.op).hom (a i)) :=
  (Finsupp.smul_single _ _ _).trans (by rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_one]; rfl)

/-- Restricting along `h` the basis element of `freeOn O U` indexed by `g` gives the basis
element indexed by `h.unop ≫ g`. -/
lemma freeOn_map_freeMk {U : C} {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (h : X ⟶ Y) (g : X.unop ⟶ U) :
    (freeOn O U).map h
        (ModuleCat.freeMk (ULift.up g : (uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj X) : (freeOn O U).obj X) =
      (ModuleCat.freeMk (ULift.up (h.unop ≫ g) : (uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj Y) :
        (freeOn O U).obj Y) := by
  rw [PresheafOfModules.freeObj_map]
  exact ModuleCat.freeDesc_apply _ _

/-- Restricting `relGen a X g i` along `h` gives `relGen a Y (h.unop ≫ g) i`. -/
lemma freeOn_map_relGen {U : C} {n : ℕ} (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (h : X ⟶ Y) (g : X.unop ⟶ U) (i : Fin n) :
    (freeOn O U).map h (relGen a X g i) = relGen a Y (h.unop ≫ g) i := by
  have hc : ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map h).hom (((ringPresheaf O.obj).map g.op).hom (a i))
      = ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map (h.unop ≫ g).op).hom (a i) := by
    rw [show ((h.unop ≫ g).op : op U ⟶ Y) = g.op ≫ h from rfl,
      (ringPresheaf O.obj).map_comp]
    rfl
  refine (PresheafOfModules.map_smul _ h _ _).trans ?_
  rw [freeOn_map_freeMk, hc]
  rfl

/-- The subpresheaf of `freeOn O U` which, over `X`, is generated in the component indexed by
`g : X ⟶ U` by the restrictions of `a` along `g`. -/
noncomputable def relSubmodule {U : C} {n : ℕ}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)) : (freeOn O U).Submodule where
  obj X := Submodule.span ((ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X)
    (Set.range fun p : (X.unop ⟶ U) × Fin n ↦ relGen a X p.1 p.2)
  map {X Y} f := by
    refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨p, rfl⟩
    refine Submodule.mem_comap.mpr ?_
    change (freeOn O U).map f (relGen a X p.1 p.2) ∈ _
    rw [freeOn_map_relGen]
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨(f.unop ≫ p.1, p.2), rfl⟩

/-- Each `relGen a X g i` is a section of `relSubmodule a` over `X`. -/
lemma relGen_mem {U : C} {n : ℕ} (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) (g : X.unop ⟶ U) (i : Fin n) :
    relGen a X g i ∈ (relSubmodule a).obj X :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨(g, i), rfl⟩

/-- Over `U` itself, the generator attached to the identity arrow is `a i` times the basis
element indexed by the identity. -/
lemma relGen_id {U : C} {n : ℕ} (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)) (i : Fin n) :
    relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i
      = a i • (ModuleCat.freeMk (ULift.up (𝟙 U) : (uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj (op U)) :
          (freeOn O U).obj (op U)) := by
  rw [relGen]
  congr 1
  rw [show ((𝟙 U).op : op U ⟶ op U) = 𝟙 (op U) from rfl, (ringPresheaf O.obj).map_id]
  rfl

/-- Restricting along `f : V ⟶ U` the generator attached to the identity arrow of `U` gives the
generator attached to `f`, as a section of `relSubmodule a`. -/
lemma relSubmodule_map_relGen_id {U V : C} {n : ℕ}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)) (f : V ⟶ U) (i : Fin n) :
    ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).map f.op
        (⟨relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i, relGen_mem a (op U) (𝟙 U) i⟩ :
          ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op U))
      = (⟨relGen a (op V) f i, relGen_mem a (op V) f i⟩ :
          ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op V)) :=
  Subtype.ext ((freeOn_map_relGen a f.op (𝟙 U) i).trans
    (congrArg (fun g ↦ relGen a (op V) g i) (Category.comp_id f)))

/-- Over `X`, the sub-`O`-module `relSubmodule a` is spanned by the `relGen`. -/
lemma span_relGen_mk_eq_top {U : C} {n : ℕ} (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Submodule.span ((ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) (Set.range fun p : (X.unop ⟶ U) × Fin n ↦
        (⟨relGen a X p.1 p.2, relGen_mem a X p.1 p.2⟩ : (relSubmodule a).obj X)) = ⊤ :=
  span_range_mk_eq_top _

end Construction

section LocalStep

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{max v w}}

/-- The coefficient of a section of `freeOn O U` in the component indexed by `f : X ⟶ U`. -/
noncomputable def relCoeff {U : C} (X : Cᵒᵖ) (f : X.unop ⟶ U) :
    (freeOn O U).obj X →ₗ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X] (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X :=
  show ((uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj X →₀ (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) →ₗ[_] _ from
    Finsupp.lapply (ULift.up f)

/-- Projection of `freeOn O U` onto the component indexed by a fixed `f : X ⟶ U`. -/
noncomputable def relProj {U : C} (X : Cᵒᵖ) (f : X.unop ⟶ U) :
    (freeOn O U).obj X →ₗ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X] (freeOn O U).obj X :=
  show ((uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj X →₀ (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) →ₗ[_]
      ((uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj X →₀ (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) from
    (Finsupp.lsingle (ULift.up f)).comp (Finsupp.lapply (ULift.up f))

/-- The `f`-coefficient of `relGen a X f i` is the restriction of `a i` along `f`. -/
lemma relCoeff_relGen_self {U : C} {n : ℕ} (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) (f : X.unop ⟶ U) (i : Fin n) :
    relCoeff X f (relGen a X f i) = ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map f.op).hom (a i) := by
  rw [relGen_eq_single]
  exact Finsupp.single_eq_same

/-- The projection onto the `f`-component fixes `relGen a X f i`. -/
lemma relProj_relGen_self {U : C} {n : ℕ} (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) (f : X.unop ⟶ U) (i : Fin n) :
    relProj X f (relGen a X f i) = relGen a X f i := by
  rw [relGen_eq_single]
  exact congrArg (Finsupp.single (ULift.up f : (uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj X))
    Finsupp.single_eq_same

/-- The projection onto the `f`-component kills `relGen a X g i` for `g ≠ f`. -/
lemma relProj_relGen_of_ne {U : C} {n : ℕ} (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) (f g : X.unop ⟶ U) (i : Fin n) (hgf : g ≠ f) :
    relProj X f (relGen a X g i) = 0 := by
  have h0 : (Finsupp.single (ULift.up g : (uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj X)
        (((ringPresheaf O.obj).map g.op).hom (a i)))
      (ULift.up f : (uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj X) = 0 :=
    Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne (fun hc ↦ hgf (congrArg ULift.down hc).symm)
  exact (congrArg (relProj X f) (relGen_eq_single a X g i)).trans
    ((congrArg (Finsupp.single (ULift.up f : (uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj X)) h0).trans
      (Finsupp.single_zero _))

/-- The projection onto the `f`-component maps the sections of `relSubmodule a` into the
submodule generated by the `f`-component generators. -/
lemma relProj_mem_span {U : C} {n : ℕ} (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) (f : X.unop ⟶ U) {x : (freeOn O U).obj X} (hx : x ∈ (relSubmodule a).obj X) :
    relProj X f x ∈ Submodule.span ((ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X)
      (Set.range fun i : Fin n ↦ relGen a X f i) := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := hy
    by_cases hp : p.1 = f
    · subst hp
      rw [relProj_relGen_self]
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨p.2, rfl⟩
    · rw [relProj_relGen_of_ne a X f p.1 p.2 hp]
      exact zero_mem _
  | zero => simp
  | add y z hy hz ihy ihz =>
    rw [map_add]
    exact add_mem ihy ihz
  | smul r y hy ih =>
    rw [map_smul]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ r ih

/-- **The local algebraic step.** If the relation element vanishes in
`relSubmodule a ⊗ F` over `X`, then `s` factors through a finite free module by a matrix
annihilating the restricted relation. -/
lemma exists_relFactorization {U : C} {n : ℕ}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    {F : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)}
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) (f : X.unop ⟶ U) (s : Fin n → F.obj X)
    (h : ∑ i, (⟨relGen a X f i, relGen_mem a X f i⟩ :
        ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj X) ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X] s i = 0) :
    ∃ (l : ℕ) (t : Fin l → F.obj X) (B : Fin l → Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X),
      (∀ i, s i = ∑ k, B k i • t k) ∧
      (∀ k, ∑ i, B k i * ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map f.op).hom (a i) = 0) := by
  exact exists_factorization_of_retraction ((relSubmodule a).obj X) (fun i ↦ relGen a X f i)
    (relGen_mem a X f · ·) (relProj X f) (relCoeff X f) _ (relProj_relGen_self a X f)
    (fun _ hy ↦ relProj_mem_span a X f hy) (relCoeff_relGen_self a X f) s h

/-- **The relation element dies in the free presheaf.** The sum `∑ᵢ gᵢ ⊗ sᵢ`, where `gᵢ` are the
generators of `relSubmodule a` attached to the identity arrow of `U`, is sent to zero by the
inclusion of `relSubmodule a` into `freeOn O U` tensored with `F`, precisely because
`∑ᵢ aᵢ • sᵢ = 0`. -/
lemma tensorRight_map_ι_app_eq_zero {U : C} {n : ℕ}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    {F : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)} (s : Fin n → F.obj (op U))
    (h : ∑ i, a i • s i = 0) :
    ((tensorRight F).map (relSubmodule a).ι).app (op U)
        (∑ i, (⟨relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i, relGen_mem a (op U) (𝟙 U) i⟩ :
          ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op U))
          ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] s i) = 0 := by
  refine (map_sum _ _ _).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_)
    (sum_smul_tmul_eq_zero a
      (ModuleCat.freeMk (ULift.up (𝟙 U) : (uliftYoneda.{w} U).obj (op U)) :
        (freeOn O U).obj (op U)) s h)
  refine (tensorRight_map_app_tmul F (relSubmodule a).ι (op U) _ (s i)).trans ?_
  exact congrArg (fun z ↦ z ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] s i) (relGen_id a i)

/-- Restriction of the relation element along `f : V ⟶ U` is the relation element attached to
`f` and the restricted sections. -/
lemma tensorObj_map_sum_relGen_tmul {U V : C} {n : ℕ}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    {F : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)} (s : Fin n → F.obj (op U))
    (f : V ⟶ U) :
    (tensorObj ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules) F).map f.op
        (∑ i, (⟨relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i, relGen_mem a (op U) (𝟙 U) i⟩ :
          ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op U))
          ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] s i)
      = ∑ i, (⟨relGen a (op V) f i, relGen_mem a (op V) f i⟩ :
          ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op V))
          ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)] F.map f.op (s i) := by
  refine (map_sum _ _ _).trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_)
  refine (tensorObj_map_tmul ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules) F f.op _ (s i)).trans ?_
  exact congrArg (fun z ↦ z ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)] F.map f.op (s i))
    (relSubmodule_map_relGen_id a f i)

/-- If tensoring with `F` keeps `ι : P ⟶ Q` locally injective, an element of `P ⊗ F` over `U` killed
by `ι` is killed on the covering equalizer sieve, where any property deduced from vanishing
holds. -/
private theorem exists_sieve_of_isLocallyInjective {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w}}
    {P Q F : PresheafOfModules.{w} (ringPresheaf R)} (ι : P ⟶ Q)
    (hu : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf R)).map ((tensorRight F).map ι)))
    {U : C} (z : (tensorObj P F).obj (op U)) (hz : ((tensorRight F).map ι).app (op U) z = 0)
    (T : ∀ ⦃V : C⦄, (V ⟶ U) → Prop)
    (hT : ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (f : V ⟶ U), (tensorObj P F).map f.op z = 0 → T f) :
    ∃ S : Sieve U, S ∈ J U ∧ ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (f : V ⟶ U), S f → T f :=
  ⟨Presheaf.equalizerSieve
      (F := (PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf R)).obj (tensorObj P F)) (X := op U) z 0,
    Presheaf.equalizerSieve_mem J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf R)).map ((tensorRight F).map ι)) z 0
      (hz.trans (map_zero _).symm),
    fun _ f hf ↦ hT f (hf.trans (map_zero _))⟩

/-- **The local step, spread over a covering.** If tensoring with `F` keeps the inclusion of the
relation subpresheaf locally injective, then a relation `∑ᵢ aᵢ • sᵢ = 0` over `U` admits, on a
covering sieve of `U`, a factorisation of `s` through a finite free module annihilating the
relation. The covering sieve produced is the equalizer sieve of the relation element. -/
lemma exists_covering_relFactorization {U : C} {n : ℕ}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    {F : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)} (s : Fin n → F.obj (op U))
    (h : ∑ i, a i • s i = 0)
    (hu : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map
        ((tensorRight F).map (relSubmodule a).ι))) :
    ∃ S : Sieve U, S ∈ J U ∧ ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (f : V ⟶ U), S f →
      ∃ (l : ℕ) (t : Fin l → F.obj (op V))
        (B : Fin l → Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)),
        (∀ i, F.map f.op (s i) = ∑ k, B k i • t k) ∧
        (∀ k, ∑ i, B k i * ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map f.op).hom (a i) = 0) := by
  refine exists_sieve_of_isLocallyInjective _ hu _ (tensorRight_map_ι_app_eq_zero a s h) _ ?_
  intro V f hf
  exact exists_relFactorization a (op V) f (fun i ↦ F.map f.op (s i))
    ((tensorObj_map_sum_relGen_tmul a s f).symm.trans hf)

end LocalStep

section TupleConstruction

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- The presheaf of `n`-tuples of sections of the structure sheaf. -/
@[simps]
def coeffTuples (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}) (n : ℕ) : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w where
  obj X := Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X
  map {X Y} h := ↾fun (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) ↦
    (fun i ↦ ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map h).hom (b i) : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj Y)

/-- The free presheaf of `O`-modules on the `n`-tuples of sections of the structure sheaf. -/
noncomputable abbrev freeTuples (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}) (n : ℕ) :
    PresheafOfModules.{w} (ringPresheaf O.obj) :=
  PresheafOfModules.freeObj (R := ringPresheaf O.obj) (coeffTuples O n)

variable {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}}

/-- The section of `freeTuples O n` over `X` attached to a tuple `b` of sections and an index
`i`: the basis element indexed by `b`, scaled by the `i`-th entry of `b`. -/
noncomputable def tupleGen {n : ℕ} (X : Cᵒᵖ) (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X)
    (i : Fin n) : (freeTuples O n).obj X :=
  b i • (ModuleCat.freeMk (b : (coeffTuples O n).obj X) : (freeTuples O n).obj X)

/-- `tupleGen X b i` is the finitely supported function at `b` with value `b i`. -/
lemma tupleGen_eq_single {n : ℕ} (X : Cᵒᵖ) (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) (i : Fin n) :
    tupleGen X b i = Finsupp.single (b : (coeffTuples O n).obj X) (b i) :=
  (Finsupp.smul_single _ _ _).trans (by rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_one]; rfl)

/-- Restricting along `h` the basis element of `freeTuples O n` indexed by `b` gives the basis
element indexed by the restriction of `b`. -/
lemma freeTuples_map_freeMk {n : ℕ} {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (h : X ⟶ Y) (b : (coeffTuples O n).obj X) :
    (freeTuples O n).map h (ModuleCat.freeMk b : (freeTuples O n).obj X) =
      (ModuleCat.freeMk ((coeffTuples O n).map h b) : (freeTuples O n).obj Y) := by
  rw [PresheafOfModules.freeObj_map]
  exact ModuleCat.freeDesc_apply _ _

/-- Restricting `tupleGen X b i` along `h` gives the generator attached to the restriction of
`b` and the same index `i`. -/
lemma freeTuples_map_tupleGen {n : ℕ} {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (h : X ⟶ Y)
    (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) (i : Fin n) :
    (freeTuples O n).map h (tupleGen X b i)
      = tupleGen Y (fun j ↦ ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map h).hom (b j)) i :=
  (PresheafOfModules.map_smul _ h _ _).trans
    (congrArg (fun z : (freeTuples O n).obj Y ↦ ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map h).hom (b i) • z)
      (freeTuples_map_freeMk h (b : (coeffTuples O n).obj X)))

/-- The subpresheaf of `freeTuples O n` which, over `X`, is generated by the sections
`tupleGen X b i` for every tuple `b` of sections over `X` and every index `i`. -/
noncomputable def tupleSubmodule (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}) (n : ℕ) :
    (freeTuples O n).Submodule where
  obj X := Submodule.span ((ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X)
    (Set.range fun p : (Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) × Fin n ↦ tupleGen X p.1 p.2)
  map {X Y} h := by
    refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨p, rfl⟩
    refine Submodule.mem_comap.mpr ?_
    change (freeTuples O n).map h (tupleGen X p.1 p.2) ∈ _
    rw [freeTuples_map_tupleGen]
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨(fun j ↦ ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map h).hom (p.1 j), p.2), rfl⟩

/-- Each `tupleGen X b i` is a section of `tupleSubmodule O n` over `X`. -/
lemma tupleGen_mem {n : ℕ} (X : Cᵒᵖ) (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) (i : Fin n) :
    tupleGen X b i ∈ (tupleSubmodule O n).obj X :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨(b, i), rfl⟩

/-- Restricting the generator attached to `b` along `f` gives the generator attached to the
restriction of `b`, as a section of `tupleSubmodule O n`. -/
lemma tupleSubmodule_map_tupleGen {n : ℕ} {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (h : X ⟶ Y)
    (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) (i : Fin n) :
    ((tupleSubmodule O n).toPresheafOfModules).map h
        (⟨tupleGen X b i, tupleGen_mem X b i⟩ :
          ((tupleSubmodule O n).toPresheafOfModules).obj X)
      = (⟨tupleGen Y (fun j ↦ ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map h).hom (b j)) i,
          tupleGen_mem Y _ i⟩ : ((tupleSubmodule O n).toPresheafOfModules).obj Y) :=
  Subtype.ext (freeTuples_map_tupleGen h b i)

/-- Over `X`, the sub-`O`-module `tupleSubmodule O n` is spanned by the `tupleGen`. -/
lemma span_tupleGen_mk_eq_top (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}) (n : ℕ) (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Submodule.span ((ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X)
        (Set.range fun p : (Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) × Fin n ↦
          (⟨tupleGen X p.1 p.2, tupleGen_mem X p.1 p.2⟩ : (tupleSubmodule O n).obj X)) = ⊤ :=
  span_range_mk_eq_top _

end TupleConstruction

section TupleLocalStep

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}}

/-- The coefficient of a section of `freeTuples O n` in the component indexed by the tuple
`b`. -/
noncomputable def tupleCoeff {n : ℕ} (X : Cᵒᵖ) (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) :
    (freeTuples O n).obj X →ₗ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X] (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X :=
  show ((coeffTuples O n).obj X →₀ (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) →ₗ[_] _ from
    Finsupp.lapply (b : (coeffTuples O n).obj X)

/-- Projection of `freeTuples O n` onto the component indexed by the tuple `b`. -/
noncomputable def tupleProj {n : ℕ} (X : Cᵒᵖ) (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) :
    (freeTuples O n).obj X →ₗ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X] (freeTuples O n).obj X :=
  show ((coeffTuples O n).obj X →₀ (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) →ₗ[_]
      ((coeffTuples O n).obj X →₀ (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) from
    (Finsupp.lsingle (b : (coeffTuples O n).obj X)).comp
      (Finsupp.lapply (b : (coeffTuples O n).obj X))

/-- The `b`-coefficient of `tupleGen X b i` is `b i`. -/
lemma tupleCoeff_tupleGen_self {n : ℕ} (X : Cᵒᵖ) (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X)
    (i : Fin n) : tupleCoeff X b (tupleGen X b i) = b i := by
  rw [tupleGen_eq_single]
  exact Finsupp.single_eq_same

/-- The projection onto the `b`-component fixes `tupleGen X b i`. -/
lemma tupleProj_tupleGen_self {n : ℕ} (X : Cᵒᵖ) (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X)
    (i : Fin n) : tupleProj X b (tupleGen X b i) = tupleGen X b i := by
  rw [tupleGen_eq_single]
  exact congrArg (Finsupp.single (b : (coeffTuples O n).obj X)) Finsupp.single_eq_same

/-- The projection onto the `b`-component kills `tupleGen X c i` for `c ≠ b`. -/
lemma tupleProj_tupleGen_of_ne {n : ℕ} (X : Cᵒᵖ)
    (b c : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) (i : Fin n) (hcb : c ≠ b) :
    tupleProj X b (tupleGen X c i) = 0 := by
  have h0 : (Finsupp.single (c : (coeffTuples O n).obj X) (c i))
      (b : (coeffTuples O n).obj X) = 0 :=
    Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne (Ne.symm hcb)
  exact (congrArg (tupleProj X b) (tupleGen_eq_single X c i)).trans
    ((congrArg (Finsupp.single (b : (coeffTuples O n).obj X)) h0).trans (Finsupp.single_zero _))

/-- The projection onto the `b`-component maps the sections of `tupleSubmodule O n` into the
submodule generated by the `b`-component generators. -/
lemma tupleProj_mem_span {n : ℕ} (X : Cᵒᵖ) (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X)
    {x : (freeTuples O n).obj X} (hx : x ∈ (tupleSubmodule O n).obj X) :
    tupleProj X b x ∈ Submodule.span ((ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X)
      (Set.range fun i : Fin n ↦ tupleGen X b i) := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := hy
    by_cases hp : p.1 = b
    · subst hp
      rw [tupleProj_tupleGen_self]
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨p.2, rfl⟩
    · rw [tupleProj_tupleGen_of_ne X b p.1 p.2 hp]
      exact zero_mem _
  | zero => simp
  | add y z hy hz ihy ihz =>
    rw [map_add]
    exact add_mem ihy ihz
  | smul r y hy ih =>
    rw [map_smul]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ r ih

/-- **The local algebraic step, universal form.** If the relation element attached to the tuple
`b` vanishes in `tupleSubmodule O n ⊗ F` over `X`, then `s` factors through a finite free module
by a matrix annihilating `b`. -/
lemma exists_tupleFactorization {n : ℕ} {F : PresheafOfModules.{w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)}
    (X : Cᵒᵖ) (b : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X) (s : Fin n → F.obj X)
    (h : ∑ i, (⟨tupleGen X b i, tupleGen_mem X b i⟩ :
        ((tupleSubmodule O n).toPresheafOfModules).obj X) ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X] s i = 0) :
    ∃ (l : ℕ) (t : Fin l → F.obj X) (B : Fin l → Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj X),
      (∀ i, s i = ∑ k, B k i • t k) ∧ (∀ k, ∑ i, B k i * b i = 0) := by
  exact exists_factorization_of_retraction ((tupleSubmodule O n).obj X) (tupleGen X b)
    (tupleGen_mem X b) (tupleProj X b) (tupleCoeff X b) b (tupleProj_tupleGen_self X b)
    (fun _ hy ↦ tupleProj_mem_span X b hy) (tupleCoeff_tupleGen_self X b) s h

/-- **The relation element dies in the free presheaf.** The sum `∑ᵢ gᵢ ⊗ sᵢ`, where `gᵢ` are the
generators of `tupleSubmodule O n` attached to the tuple `a`, is sent to zero by the inclusion of
`tupleSubmodule O n` into `freeTuples O n` tensored with `F`, precisely because
`∑ᵢ aᵢ • sᵢ = 0`. -/
lemma tensorRight_map_tupleIota_app_eq_zero {n : ℕ} {U : C}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    {F : PresheafOfModules.{w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)} (s : Fin n → F.obj (op U))
    (h : ∑ i, a i • s i = 0) :
    ((tensorRight F).map (tupleSubmodule O n).ι).app (op U)
        (∑ i, (⟨tupleGen (op U) a i, tupleGen_mem (op U) a i⟩ :
          ((tupleSubmodule O n).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op U))
          ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] s i) = 0 := by
  refine (map_sum _ _ _).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_)
    (sum_smul_tmul_eq_zero a
      (ModuleCat.freeMk (a : (coeffTuples O n).obj (op U)) : (freeTuples O n).obj (op U)) s h)
  exact tensorRight_map_app_tmul F (tupleSubmodule O n).ι (op U) _ (s i)

/-- Restriction of the relation element along `f : V ⟶ U` is the relation element attached to the
restricted tuple and the restricted sections. -/
lemma tensorObj_map_sum_tupleGen_tmul {n : ℕ} {U V : C}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    {F : PresheafOfModules.{w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)} (s : Fin n → F.obj (op U)) (f : V ⟶ U) :
    (tensorObj ((tupleSubmodule O n).toPresheafOfModules) F).map f.op
        (∑ i, (⟨tupleGen (op U) a i, tupleGen_mem (op U) a i⟩ :
          ((tupleSubmodule O n).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op U))
          ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] s i)
      = ∑ i, (⟨tupleGen (op V) (fun j ↦ ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map f.op).hom (a j)) i,
          tupleGen_mem (op V) _ i⟩ : ((tupleSubmodule O n).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op V))
          ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)] F.map f.op (s i) := by
  refine (map_sum _ _ _).trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_)
  refine (tensorObj_map_tmul ((tupleSubmodule O n).toPresheafOfModules) F f.op _ (s i)).trans ?_
  exact congrArg (fun z ↦ z ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)] F.map f.op (s i))
    (tupleSubmodule_map_tupleGen f.op a i)

/-- **The local step, spread over a covering.** If tensoring with `F` keeps the inclusion of the
universal relation subpresheaf locally injective, then a relation `∑ᵢ aᵢ • sᵢ = 0` over `U`
admits, on a covering sieve of `U`, a factorisation of `s` through a finite free module
annihilating the relation. The covering sieve produced is the equalizer sieve of the relation
element. -/
lemma exists_covering_tupleFactorization {n : ℕ} {U : C}
    (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
    {F : PresheafOfModules.{w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)} (s : Fin n → F.obj (op U))
    (h : ∑ i, a i • s i = 0)
    (hu : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map
        ((tensorRight F).map (tupleSubmodule O n).ι))) :
    ∃ S : Sieve U, S ∈ J U ∧ ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (f : V ⟶ U), S f →
      ∃ (l : ℕ) (t : Fin l → F.obj (op V))
        (B : Fin l → Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)),
        (∀ i, F.map f.op (s i) = ∑ k, B k i • t k) ∧
        (∀ k, ∑ i, B k i * ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map f.op).hom (a i) = 0) := by
  refine exists_sieve_of_isLocallyInjective _ hu _ (tensorRight_map_tupleIota_app_eq_zero a s h) _
    ?_
  intro V f hf
  exact exists_tupleFactorization (op V)
    (fun j ↦ ((ringPresheaf O.obj).map f.op).hom (a j)) (fun i ↦ F.map f.op (s i))
    ((tensorObj_map_sum_tupleGen_tmul a s f).symm.trans hf)

end TupleLocalStep

section Flat

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] in
/-- A monomorphism of sheaves of modules is injective on sections. -/
lemma injective_val_app_of_mono {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}
    {M N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} R} (u : M ⟶ N) [Mono u] (X : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Function.Injective (u.val.app X) :=
  PresheafOfModules.injective_of_mono ((_root_.SheafOfModules.forget R).map u) X

variable (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w})

/-- Sheafification of presheaves of `O`-modules. -/
noncomputable abbrev shf := PresheafOfModules.sheafification (R := commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)
    (𝟙 (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj)

/-- The right adjoint of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shf`. -/
noncomputable abbrev shfRight := _root_.SheafOfModules.forget (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O) ⋙
  PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars (𝟙 (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj)

/-- The sheafification adjunction for presheaves of `O`-modules. -/
noncomputable abbrev shfAdj : shf O ⊣ shfRight O :=
  PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (R := commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)
    (𝟙 (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj)

variable {O}

/-- The unit of the sheafification adjunction is locally injective. -/
instance isLocallyInjective_shfAdj_unit
    (P : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ((shfAdj O).unit.app P)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J P.presheaf))

/-- The unit of the sheafification adjunction is locally surjective. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_shfAdj_unit
    (P : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ((shfAdj O).unit.app P)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J P.presheaf))

/-- Sections of a morphism of sheaves of modules which is a monomorphism are injective. -/
lemma isLocallyInjective_shfRight_map
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q)
    [Mono ((shf O).map u)] :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ((shfRight O).map ((shf O).map u))) :=
  Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_of_injective _ _
    (fun X ↦ injective_val_app_of_mono ((shf O).map u) X)

/-- Naturality of the unit of the sheafification adjunction. -/
lemma shfAdj_unit_naturality
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q) :
    u ≫ (shfAdj O).unit.app Q
      = (shfAdj O).unit.app P ≫ (shfRight O).map ((shf O).map u) :=
  (shfAdj O).unit.naturality u

/-- A morphism of presheaves of modules whose sheafification is a monomorphism is locally
injective. -/
lemma isLocallyInjective_of_mono_shf_map
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q)
    [Mono ((shf O).map u)] :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map u) := by
  have h1 := isLocallyInjective_shfRight_map u
  rw [← Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_comp_iff J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map u)
    ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ((shfAdj O).unit.app Q)), ← Functor.map_comp,
    shfAdj_unit_naturality u, Functor.map_comp]
  infer_instance

/-- Tensoring presheaves of `O`-modules on the right by (the underlying presheaf of) a sheaf
of `O`-modules. -/
noncomputable abbrev tensorRightOf (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w})
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)) :=
  tensorRight (O := O.obj) F.val

/-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_shfAdj_unit` with the underlying presheaf of
rings spelled `Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj`, which is the spelling the tensor product uses. -/
instance isLocallyInjective_shfAdj_unit_ringPresheaf
    (P : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map ((shfAdj O).unit.app P)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J P.presheaf))

/-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallySurjective_shfAdj_unit` with the underlying presheaf of
rings spelled `Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj`, which is the spelling the tensor product uses. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_shfAdj_unit_ringPresheaf
    (P : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map ((shfAdj O).unit.app P)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J P.presheaf))

omit [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] in
/-- The right adjoint of sheafification acts on morphisms by taking the underlying morphism of
presheaves of modules. -/
lemma shfRight_map_eq {M N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)}
    (u : M ⟶ N) : (shfRight O).map u = u.val :=
  PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun _ ↦ rfl

omit [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] in
/-- The identity, read as the comparison morphism from `Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj` to the
underlying presheaf of `Stacks.commRingSheafToRingSheaf O`, is locally injective. Recorded as an
instance because typeclass search cannot cross between the two spellings on its own. -/
instance isLocallyInjective_id_commRingSheafToRingSheaf :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      (show ringPresheaf O.obj ⟶ (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj from
        𝟙 (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) :=
  Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_of_injective _ _ fun _ _ _ h ↦ h

omit [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] in
/-- The companion of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_id_commRingSheafToRingSheaf` for
local surjectivity. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_id_commRingSheafToRingSheaf :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J
      (show ringPresheaf O.obj ⟶ (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj from
        𝟙 (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) :=
  Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_surjective _ _ fun _ x ↦ ⟨x, rfl⟩

/-- **Sheafification preserves monomorphisms of presheaves of modules.** A monomorphism is
injective on sections, hence locally injective, and sheafification of a locally injective
morphism is a monomorphism of sheaves.

This is deduced from `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.mono_of_isLocallyInjective` rather than from
`PreservesFiniteLimits (PresheafOfModules.sheafification _)`, because the latter is available
only under `HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat` while the former needs nothing beyond the hypotheses of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsFlat`. -/
lemma mono_shf_map {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj}
    (u : P ⟶ Q) (hu : Mono u) : Mono ((shf O).map u) := by
  have := hu
  have h1 : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj).map u) :=
    Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_of_injective _ _
      fun X ↦ PresheafOfModules.injective_of_mono u X
  have h2 : Sheaf.IsLocallyInjective ((presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w}).map
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj).map u)) :=
    (Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_presheafToSheaf_map_iff J _).2 h1
  have h3 : Mono ((presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w}).map
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj).map u)) :=
    Sheaf.mono_of_isLocallyInjective _
  have h4 : Mono ((_root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)).map
      ((shf O).map u)) := h3
  exact (_root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)).mono_of_mono_map h4

/-- The unit of the sheafification adjunction, with its target spelled as the underlying
presheaf of modules of the sheafification instead of as the value of the right adjoint. The two
are equal by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shfRight_map_eq`, but the spelling without
`PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars` is the one that the objectwise tensor product can be
applied to at an affordable cost. -/
noncomputable def shfUnit (P : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) :
    P ⟶ ((shf O).obj P).val :=
  (shfAdj O).unit.app P

/-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shfUnit` is locally injective, with the underlying presheaf of rings
spelled `Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj`. -/
instance isLocallyInjective_shfUnit
    (P : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map (shfUnit P)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J P.presheaf))

/-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shfUnit` is locally surjective, with the underlying presheaf of rings
spelled `Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj`. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_shfUnit
    (P : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map (shfUnit P)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J P.presheaf))

/-- Naturality of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shfUnit`. -/
lemma shfUnit_naturality
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q) :
    u ≫ shfUnit Q = shfUnit P ≫ ((shf O).map u).val := by
  have h := shfAdj_unit_naturality u
  rwa [shfRight_map_eq] at h

/-- The naturality square of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shfUnit` after tensoring with `F` and
sheafifying. -/
lemma square_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O))
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q) :
    (shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map u) ≫
        (shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map (shfUnit Q))
      = (shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map (shfUnit P)) ≫
        (shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map (((shf O).map u).val)) :=
  functor_map_square (D := PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj)
    (tensorRightOf O F) (shf O) (shfUnit_naturality u)

/-- Tensoring with `F` and sheafifying inverts the unit of the sheafification adjunction. This
is `Stacks.isIso_sheafification_map_tensorRight_map` specialised to the sheafification of
presheaves of `O`-modules. -/
instance isIso_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map_shfUnit
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O))
    (P : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) :
    IsIso ((shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map (shfUnit P))) :=
  isIso_sheafification_map_tensorRight_map (O := O.obj) (R := commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)
    (N := F.val) (𝟙 (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) (shfUnit P)

/-- For a flat `F`, tensoring with `F` and sheafifying preserves monomorphisms *of sheaves* of
modules. This is flatness used literally: the sheaf-level tensor functor
`(Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor O).flip.obj F` is exact, hence preserves finite
limits, hence monomorphisms, and its value at `v` is `shf ∘ tensorRightOf` applied to `v.val`
by definition. -/
lemma mono_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map_val
    {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)} (hF : IsFlat F)
    {M N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)} (v : M ⟶ N) [Mono v] :
    Mono ((shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map v.val)) := by
  have : Limits.PreservesFiniteLimits
      ((Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} O).flip.obj F) := hF.1
  have : ((Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} O).flip.obj F).PreservesMonomorphisms :=
    inferInstance
  exact @Functor.map_mono _ _ _ _ ((Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} O).flip.obj F) this
    _ _ v ‹Mono v›

/-- For a flat `F`, tensoring with `F` and sheafifying preserves monomorphisms *of presheaves*
of modules. The other two edges of the naturality square of the sheafification unit are handled
by the two previous results: the unit at the source becomes an isomorphism and the sheafified
morphism a monomorphism.

The monomorphism hypothesis is an explicit argument, not an instance: the caller has it at the
`Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj` spelling of the underlying presheaf of rings, and typeclass search
does not cross between the two spellings. -/
lemma mono_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map
    {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)} (hF : IsFlat F)
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q)
    (hu : Mono u) :
    Mono ((shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map u)) :=
  have := mono_shf_map u hu
  mono_of_square (square_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map F u) inferInstance
    (mono_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map_val hF ((shf O).map u))

/-- A flat sheaf of modules satisfies the single-relation form of the local equational criterion:
every relation `∑ᵢ aᵢ • sᵢ = 0` among its sections over an object `U` admits, on a covering sieve
of `U`, a factorisation of the restricted sections through a finite free module by a matrix
annihilating the restricted relation. The universe `w` of the sections of the structure sheaf is
independent of the universes of the site. -/
@[stacks 08FC "part (1) implies part (2)", sga "4 V 8.2.11" "(a), special case"]
theorem hasLocalSingleRelationFactorizations_of_isFlat_freeUniverse
    {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)} (hF : IsFlat F) :
    HasLocalSingleRelationFactorizations O F := by
  intro U n a s h
  have hmono : Mono (tupleSubmodule O n).ι := inferInstance
  have hloc : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map
        ((tensorRightOf O F).map (tupleSubmodule O n).ι)) :=
    have := mono_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map hF (tupleSubmodule O n).ι hmono
    isLocallyInjective_of_mono_shf_map ((tensorRightOf O F).map (tupleSubmodule O n).ι)
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hfac⟩ := exists_covering_tupleFactorization a (F := F.val) s h hloc
  exact ⟨S, hS, fun f hf ↦
    let ⟨l, t, B, h1, h2⟩ := hfac f hf
    ⟨l, t, B, h1, fun k _ ↦ h2 k⟩⟩

end Flat

end Stacks.SheafOfModules
